# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  THE CSP MUST LIST EVERY THIRD PARTY THE PAGE LOADS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  The previous policy allowed scripts from 'self' and https://va.vercel-scripts.com
#  only — a leftover from Vercel that this project no longer uses. That silently
#  blocked Clerk:
#
#      Loading the script violates the following Content Security Policy
#      directive: "script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' ..."
#      Failed to load Clerk JS (code="failed_to_load_clerk_js")
#
#  Clerk never initialised, so sign-in and sign-up could not work at all, and the
#  browser reported it only in the console. Verifying the domain in Clerk and
#  fixing DNS cannot help while the browser refuses to fetch the script.
#
#  Anything third-party added later — a script, an image host, an API — has to be
#  listed here too, or it fails the same silent way.
#
#  What each Clerk-related origin is for:
#    clerk.homeofcalculators.com  Clerk's JS bundle and Frontend API
#    *.clerk.accounts.dev         the development instance, for local/preview work
#    challenges.cloudflare.com    Turnstile, Clerk's bot protection on sign-up
#    worker-src blob:             Clerk spawns a web worker from a blob URL
#    frame-src                    Turnstile widget and Clerk-hosted flows
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  WHY THIS IS ONE RULE AND NOT PER-PATH
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Cloudflare Pages APPENDS the headers of every matching rule rather than
#  letting a more specific one win. Two matching rules means the browser gets two
#  Content-Security-Policy headers, and it then enforces the INTERSECTION — the
#  strictest value of each directive across both.
#
#  So a `/*` rule with `frame-ancestors 'self'` plus an `/embed/*` rule with
#  `frame-ancestors *` does NOT make embeds framable. The intersection is 'self',
#  and every calculator embedded on a customer's site silently stops rendering.
#
#  `frame-ancestors *` therefore has to be global. Embedding calculators into
#  other people's websites is the product, so it cannot be restricted here. The
#  cost is that the rest of the site is also framable; anything genuinely
#  sensitive should not rely on framing protection alone.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://clerk.homeofcalculators.com https://*.clerk.accounts.dev https://challenges.cloudflare.com; script-src-elem 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://clerk.homeofcalculators.com https://*.clerk.accounts.dev https://challenges.cloudflare.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data: https: blob:; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https: wss:; frame-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://clerk.homeofcalculators.com; form-action 'self' https://clerk.homeofcalculators.com; frame-ancestors *;
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
